{
  "slug": "reflexivos",
  "number": 10,
  "part": 3,
  "level": "A2",
  "title": "Reflexive verbs",
  "tagline": "Me levanto, te duchas, se llama: the daily routine and verbs with se.",
  "goal": "Conjugate reflexive verbs, place the pronoun correctly (before the verb or attached), and recognize verbs that change meaning with se.",
  "minutes": 10,
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "formas",
      "title": "The pronoun goes with the verb",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Reflexive verbs end in **-se** in the dictionary (*levantarse*). The *se* changes with the person and goes **before** the conjugated verb:"
        },
        {
          "type": "conjugation",
          "persons": ["yo", "tú", "él / ella / usted", "nosotros", "ellos / ellas / ustedes"],
          "verbs": [
            { "verb": "levantarse", "meaning": "to get up", "forms": ["{me} levanto", "{te} levantas", "{se} levanta", "{nos} levantamos", "{se} levantan"] },
            { "verb": "vestirse", "meaning": "to get dressed (e → i)", "forms": ["{me} visto", "{te} vistes", "{se} viste", "{nos} vestimos", "{se} visten"] }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "tip",
          "text": "With an infinitive or a gerund, the pronoun can also go at the end: *Me voy a duchar = Voy a duchar{me}. Me estoy vistiendo = Estoy vistiéndo{me}.*"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "rutina",
      "title": "The daily routine",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Verb", "English"],
          "rows": [
            ["*despertarse (e → ie)*", "to wake up"],
            ["*levantarse*", "to get up"],
            ["*ducharse / bañarse*", "to shower / to bathe (to shower, in much of Latin America)"],
            ["*lavarse los dientes, cepillarse*", "to brush (teeth, hair)"],
            ["*vestirse (e → i)*", "to get dressed"],
            ["*arreglarse*", "to get ready"],
            ["*acostarse (o → ue)*", "to go to bed"],
            ["*dormirse (o → ue)*", "to fall asleep"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "tone": "warning",
          "title": "No «my» with the body",
          "text": "*Me lavo {las} manos* (I wash my hands), never «me lavo mis manos». The reflexive pronoun already says whose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "significado",
      "title": "Se changes the meaning",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "head": ["Without se", "With se"],
          "rows": [
            ["*ir* = to go", "*irse* = to leave"],
            ["*dormir* = to sleep", "*dormirse* = to fall asleep"],
            ["*llamar* = to call", "*llamarse* = to be called"],
            ["*quedar* = to arrange to meet", "*quedarse* = to stay"],
            ["*poner* = to put", "*ponerse* = to put on (clothes), to become"],
            ["*acordar* = to agree", "*acordarse de* = to remember"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "examples",
          "items": [
            { "fr": "Nos {vemos} mañana.", "tr": "See you tomorrow.", "note": "reciprocal: each other" },
            { "fr": "Ana y Luis {se quieren} mucho.", "tr": "Ana and Luis love each other a lot." }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "conjuga",
      "section": "formas",
      "title": "Conjugate",
      "instructions": "Write the reflexive verb in the present, with its pronoun.",
      "kind": "type",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "Yo ___ a las seis. (levantarse)", "answer": "me levanto" },
        { "prompt": "¿A qué hora ___ tú? (acostarse)", "answer": "te acuestas" },
        { "prompt": "Mi hermano ___ muy rápido. (vestirse)", "answer": "se viste" },
        { "prompt": "Nosotros ___ por la noche. (ducharse)", "answer": "nos duchamos" },
        { "prompt": "Ellos ___ temprano. (despertarse)", "answer": "se despiertan" },
        { "prompt": "¿Cómo ___ usted? (llamarse)", "answer": "se llama" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "posicion",
      "section": "formas",
      "title": "Where does the pronoun go?",
      "instructions": "Choose the correct sentence.",
      "kind": "choice",
      "speak": "answer",
      "items": [
        { "options": ["Me voy a duchar.", "Voy me a duchar.", "Voy a me duchar."], "answer": "Me voy a duchar." },
        { "options": ["Voy a ducharme.", "Voy a duchar me.", "Voy ducharme a."], "answer": "Voy a ducharme." },
        { "options": ["Me estoy vistiendo.", "Estoy me vistiendo.", "Estoy vistiendo me."], "answer": "Me estoy vistiendo." },
        { "options": ["Me lavo las manos.", "Lavo mis manos.", "Me lavo mis manos."], "answer": "Me lavo las manos." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "con-sin",
      "section": "significado",
      "title": "With or without se?",
      "instructions": "Choose the verb that fits the meaning.",
      "kind": "choice",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "Ya es tarde, ___. (I'm leaving)", "options": ["me voy", "voy"], "answer": "me voy" },
        { "prompt": "Anoche ___ viendo la tele. (I fell asleep)", "options": ["me dormí", "dormí"], "answer": "me dormí" },
        { "prompt": "Hoy ___ en casa. (I'm staying)", "options": ["me quedo", "quedo"], "answer": "me quedo" },
        { "prompt": "¿___ de mí? (Do you remember…)", "options": ["Te acuerdas", "Acuerdas"], "answer": "Te acuerdas" },
        { "prompt": "Hace frío, ___ el abrigo. (I put on)", "options": ["me pongo", "pongo"], "answer": "me pongo" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "traduce",
      "section": "final",
      "title": "Say it in Spanish",
      "instructions": "Translate.",
      "kind": "type",
      "speak": "answer",
      "items": [
        { "prompt": "I get up at seven.", "answer": "Me levanto a las siete." },
        { "prompt": "What's your name? (tú)", "answer": "¿Cómo te llamas?" },
        { "prompt": "We go to bed late.", "answer": "Nos acostamos tarde." },
        { "prompt": "I brush my teeth.", "answer": "Me lavo los dientes.", "accept": ["Me cepillo los dientes."] },
        { "prompt": "I'm leaving.", "answer": "Me voy." },
        { "prompt": "See you tomorrow.", "answer": "Nos vemos mañana." }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "checklist": [
    "I conjugate reflexive verbs with me, te, se, nos, se.",
    "I put the pronoun before the verb or attach it to an infinitive.",
    "I say me lavo las manos, not «mis manos».",
    "I know irse, dormirse, quedarse and acordarse de."
  ],
  "challenge": {
    "title": "Your routine",
    "text": "Describe your weekday routine from waking up to falling asleep with at least six reflexive verbs: *Me despierto a las seis, me levanto a las seis y diez, me ducho…*"
  }
}
